OL,3,GNEWSATerminally ill woman urging
OL,4,Acouncil tax exemption
OL,5,
OL,6,FA terminally ill woman, told she had a
OL,7,Fyear or two left to live, is urging a
OL,8,Fcouncil to exempt those nearing the end
OL,9,Fof life from paying council tax.
OL,11,FCyndi D'souza, of Carlisle, has a rare
OL,12,Fform of terminal blood cancer and said
OL,13,Fshe should not be faced with the bill
OL,14,Fand there should not be a "postcode
OL,15,Flottery" depending on where people
OL,16,Flived.
OL,18,FLocal authorities have discretionary
OL,19,Fpowers to give terminally ill people,
OL,20,Fwho have less than 12 months to live, a
OL,21,F100% council tax discount and 30 local
OL,22,Fauthorities have adopted the measure.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,402,400,260,160,0,100
